ementation separately.","evidence":["N018-E1"]},{"id":"N016","verdict":"SUPPORTED","analysis":"Policy requires at least one independent APPROVED review at the exact current SHA and no CHANGES_REQUESTED at that SHA. The review list is complete and contains one independent APPROVED review at current head h9, with no CHANGES_REQUESTED.","next_step":"Recommended (not executed): before merging, confirm the head is still h9, since any new push would invalidate the SHA-pinned approval.","evidence":["N016-E1"]},{"id":"N011","verdict":"UNKNOWN","analysis":"The classifier labels the normalized argv[0] after calling normalize_wrapper(argv). The normalize_wrapper implementation is not supplied. It cannot be determined whether 'env MODE=ci' is stripped to leave 'pytest', or how 'pytest' is then classified.","next_step":"Recommended (not executed): read normalize_wrapper and the argv[0] classification table, or review an existing unit test for the input ['env','MODE=ci','pytest','-q'].","evidence":["N011-E1"]},{"id":"N015","verdict":"CONTRADICTED","analysis":"The graph is complete. local_main L and origin_main R are siblings, both with parent A, and L is listed as a local-only commit. The histories have diverged, so updating to R is not a fast-forward, and L is unique work that must be preserved. The clean working tree does not change this.","next_step":"Recommended (not executed): preserve L first (e.g., create a backup branch at L), then choose a rebase onto or merge with origin/main. Do not reset or discard L.","evidence":["N015-E1"]},{"id":"N020","verdict":"SUPPORTED","analysis":"The file list is complete and contains only README.md and SOP.md. The diff is described as README pointer fixes and SOP wording with no executable sections, so no runtime code changed.","next_step":"Recommended (not executed): optionally spot-check that neither Markdown file is consumed by tooling as executable configuration (e.g., doc tests or embedded scripts).","evidence":["N020-E1"]}],"limitation